        "original_id": "79fc4150-66fa-59d9-85d7-7dea07ff74d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. L. C. Pompe van Meerdervoort; Leonard du Bus de Gisignies\n- Places: Bruges; Brussels; Nagasaki; Mouscron (Hainaut); Oostmalle; Japan\n- Organizations: United Kingdom of the Netherlands\n- Topics: Bakumatsu period\n\nFacts:\n- Leonard Pierre Joseph, Viscount du Bus de Gisignies, was born in Mouscron in Hainaut on 1 March 1770.\n- The United Kingdom of the Netherlands is the unofficial name for the Kingdom of the Netherlands as it existed from 1815 to 1830.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort was born in Bruges on 5 May 1829.\n- Leonard du Bus de Gisignies was a soldier and politician in the United Kingdom of the Netherlands.\n- Leonard du Bus de Gisignies died in Oostmalle on 31 May 1849.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort was a Dutch physician based in Nagasaki during the Bakumatsu period in Japan.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort died in Brussels on 7 October 1908.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
